course: dictionary
lesson: 2942
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around them show you which meaning is right. «Shake a bottle of salad dressing and the oil breaks into tiny droplets.» Here a dressing is a sauce for salad, made from oil and vinegar.
explain: «Rinse an astro burn well under cool water, cover it with a non-stick dressing, and tell an adult.» A sauce would not cover a burn, so this dressing must be a pad or bandage that protects the wound. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: The -ing form of dress is a different job again. «Getting dressed» and «dressing up» both mean putting clothes on, and «dressing up» can mean putting on costumes. A dressing-gown is a robe you wear at home, such as «his dressing-gown, on his way to bed».
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so check which one fits the sentence.
fact: A dressing can be a sauce for salad, as in «salad dressing».
fact: A dressing can be a pad or bandage that covers a wound, as in «a wound dressing».
fact: «Dressing» can also mean putting clothes on, as in «getting dressed» or «dressing up».
fact: A dressing-gown is a robe (in the UK), and a dressing-down is a telling-off.
exercise: «Shake a bottle of salad dressing and the oil breaks into tiny droplets.» What is the dressing here? | A coat you put on | Stuffing for a turkey | *A sauce for salad, made of oil and vinegar | A bandage for a cut
exercise: «Cover it with a non-stick dressing, and tell an adult.» What does dressing mean here? | A telling-off | Putting clothes on | *A pad or bandage that protects a wound | A costume for a party
exercise: «Getting dressed for school takes me ten minutes.» What does dressing mean here? | A sauce for salad | Stuffing for a chicken | A pad for a wound | *Putting clothes on
test: «Mustard helps oil droplets stay apart longer in a dressing.» What is a dressing here? | A costume | A bandage | A robe | *A sauce
test: «He is in his dressing-gown, on his way to bed.» What is a dressing-gown? | A kind of sauce | A pad for a cut | A costume for a play | *A robe you wear at home
exam: What does «dressing up» mean in «The children loved dressing up as pirates»? | Bandaging a cut | *Putting on costumes for fun | Shouting at someone | Cooking a salad
